# RSVP Forms

The RSVP form system allows you to customize what information guests provide when responding to your event invitation. Forms support bilingual content (English/Arabic) and can be tailored per guest category.

## Overview

When guests click their personalized RSVP link, they see a form customized for your event. You control:

- Which sections appear on the form
- Which fields are shown within each section
- Which fields are required vs optional
- Which categories can see specific fields

## Form Sections

The RSVP form is organized into four standard sections:

### Personal Information

Basic guest details such as preferred language for communications. Most personal information is pre-filled from the guest record.

### Travel & Logistics

Travel-related information for guests attending from out of town:

- Arrival and departure dates
- Flight details
- Hotel accommodation needs
- Airport transportation requirements

### Experience & Program

Event-specific preferences:

- Session or workshop interests
- Dietary preferences
- Special requests

### Important to Know

Critical information for event planning:

- Dietary requirements and allergies
- Accessibility needs
- Emergency contact information

## Field Types

### Standard Fields

Pre-built fields with consistent formatting and direct database storage. Standard fields are:

- Immediately queryable in reports
- Consistent across all events
- Available in predefined formats (date pickers, dropdowns, etc.)

Examples: arrival date, dietary type, accessibility needs, emergency contact.

### Custom Fields

Event-specific questions you create for unique needs. Custom fields are:

- Fully configurable (label, type, options)
- Bilingual (separate English/Arabic labels)
- Stored flexibly for each response

Examples: "Which networking session interests you?", "T-shirt size", "Company registration number".

## Bilingual Support

All form elements support English and Arabic:

- Section titles and descriptions
- Field labels and help text
- Option labels for dropdowns and radio buttons

Guests see the form in their preferred language, with automatic right-to-left formatting for Arabic.

## Getting Started

Learn how to configure your form in the [Form Configuration](/docs/rsvp-forms/form-configuration) guide, and how to add event-specific questions in the [Custom Fields](/docs/rsvp-forms/custom-fields) guide.
